TYPES.md §5.2, §13.2 (E2102): an identifier key of a map keyed by a string-literal union over a
ref that names no entry is the checker's finding only; the let is broken, never evaluated.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// An item.
record Item {
  /// Its power.
  power: Int = 1
}

/// The items.
let items: table Item = { sword {} }

/// A weight target.
type Target = ref Item | "all"

/// The weights.
let weights: {Target: Int} = { shield: 1, "all": 2 }
